<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97113" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρᾰτήγ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>act of a general</i>, esp. <i>piece of generalship,
				stratagem</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.5.22
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				12.78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.18.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				<u>Praef.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, etc.:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγήματα</span> was the title of works by Polyaenus and
			Frontinus; cf. also <i><span class="en">
				<u>BMus.Inscr.</u>
				1020
			</span></i> (Smyrna, <span class="entity">i A.D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>trick, device</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				5.2.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.755d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῶν λόγων</span>
			<i>trick</i> of speech, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				9.8
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
